  "title": "What is SCIM? A Practical Guide for B2B SaaS Teams",
  "summary": "The TL;DR * SCIM (System for Cross-domain Identity Management, pronounced like \"skim\") is an open standard (RFC 7643 / 7644) that lets an identity provider like Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, or JumpCloud automatically create, update, and deactivate user accounts in your application. * Mechanically, it's a REST API with JSON payloads. Your app exposes SCIM endpoints, and your customer's IdP calls them whenever their employee directory changes. * SAML and OIDC are the login method. SCIM is for syn",
